    "regression_hint": "Invariant: every HDFS/Hadoop path segment derived from user input (both the leaf `name`/`fileName` and the parent `currentDir`/`fullName` used to build directoryName/hdfsFileName/destHdfsFileName/dstHdfsPath passed into HadoopUtils.getHdfsFileName, getHdfsResourceFileName, getHdfsUdfFileName, mkdir, copy, copyLocalToHdfs, delete, exists) must be rejected or canonicalized so the resulting HDFS path can never resolve outside the tenant's resource root (`getHdfsResDir`/`getHdfsUdfDir`/`getHdfsTenantDir`). A correct fix must validate `currentDir` (not just `name`) in createDirectory, createResource, updateResource, and onlineCreateResource \u2014 e.g. reject any path segment equal to \"..\" (FileUtils.directoryTraversal only rejects \"/\" in a single segment, so it cannot be applied to a multi-segment currentDir as-is) \u2014 and must apply that check before fullName is used to build any Hadoop path, including the reused fullName in the internal rename/move/copy helpers. Known bypass variants the fix must also block: (a) currentDir containing \"../\" traversal segments (tested here) as well as URL-encoded or double-encoded variants if currentDir ever comes from a raw query string; (b) traversal placed in the leaf `name`/`fileName`/`fileSuffix` fields themselves via alternate encodings that survive `FileUtils.directoryTraversal` (e.g. backslashes on platforms where `File` doesn't treat \"\\\\\" as a separator, or Unicode look-alike separators); (c) traversal reintroduced via `updateResource`'s rename path, which reuses `originFullName` + new `name` without re-validating the currentDir portion; (d) the sibling `onlineCreateResource` and rename/move call sites (ResourcesServiceImpl.java ~628-651, ~1099-1127) that independently reconstruct hdfsFilename/dstHdfsPath from fullName \u2014 a fix that only patches `createDirectory` and misses these will leave the CWE-022 open on those paths.",
